# Build context for the MT5 collector image (context: ., see
# docker-compose.prod.yml). Only collector/ and deploy/docker/m1m5-mt5-collector/
# are COPYed, but without this file the WHOLE repository was sent as context
# and `COPY collector/ /app/` baked collector/.env.production -- including the
# MT5 account password -- into the image.
#
# No env file belongs in any image: every service receives its configuration at
# runtime through `env_file` in docker-compose.prod.yml.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.git
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
backend/dist
frontend/.next

# Engine B's Telegram MTProto USER session and the runtime state directory.
# The session is an authorization key equivalent to being logged in as that
# Telegram account. It is created at runtime, in a mounted volume, and must
# never be baked into an image layer -- an image layer is copied wherever the
# image goes and cannot be un-copied.
xauusd-m1m5-runtime
**/xauusd-m1m5-runtime
**/telegram-ingest-session*
